note top of SessionManager
**SABER Domain Server & Session Manager**
- Central orchestrator hosting one security domain with async/await architecture
- Manages multiple concurrent client sessions with automatic timeout and cleanup
- Multi-episode support with episode creation semaphores for resource management
- Background episode finalization with semaphore-limited concurrent health checks
- Dual protocol handlers: REST API for session/episode management, MCP API for tool execution
- Episode-scoped execution: all operations reference episode_id explicitly
- Health monitoring with manifest information and permanent environment checks
- Client-side evaluation: server stores results, client performs LLM judge evaluation
- Supports creating/active/completed episode state tracking
- Session timeout management with automatic cleanup of inactive sessions
- Permanent environment initialization through ExecutionManager
end note

note left of SessionMCPAPI
**MCP Protocol Handler**
- Hosts Model Context Protocol server for agent tool access using FastMCP
- Dynamically discovers tools from ExecutionManager via MCPToolGenerator
- Maps MCP tool calls to SessionManager command execution using headers
- Session context AND episode context obtained from HTTP headers
- Headers: X-SABER-Session-ID, X-SABER-Episode-ID, X-SABER-Orchestration-Env
- ONLY handles tool discovery and execution via MCP protocol
- Complements REST API which handles all other operations
- Uses header-based session/episode mapping instead of maintaining active state
- Episode-aware tool execution for proper sandbox isolation
end note

note right of SessionRestAPI
**REST Protocol Handler**
- FastAPI-based REST endpoints for session and episode management
- Session lifecycle: create/terminate sessions
- Episode lifecycle: create/status/end episodes with async readiness waiting
- Episode data: task, policy, steps, submission, transcript
- Message injection for orchestrated task coordination
- Evaluation endpoints: criteria retrieval, results, summaries
- Template content retrieval for client-side prompt rendering
- File upload support for evaluation context
- All /api/v1 prefixed endpoints
- NO benchmark orchestration - client responsibility
- Delegates all business logic to SessionManager
end note

note top of BenchmarkManager
**Task Definition Manager with Prompt Generation**
- Focuses purely on task definition management and YAML parsing
- NO server-side benchmark orchestration - client responsibility
- Task objects contain execution_config, episode_config, evaluation_config
- Four-prompt system: instruction, assistant, submit, continue templates
- Validates all templates at startup (fail-fast)
- Environment can be string reference or dict config
- BenchmarkConfigLoader handles YAML parsing from directory structure
- PromptGenerator handles Jinja2 template rendering
- Supports template tasks with is_template and dependency_template fields
- Role-based task configuration for orchestrated evaluations
- Injects judge prompt renderers for llm_judge evaluation tasks
end note

note top of EpisodeManager
**RL-Style Episode Manager with Dependency Support**
- Manages gym-compatible episode lifecycle with automatic termination
- Episode-scoped operations: all methods now use episode_id instead of session_id
- Returns StepResult objects from step() method containing termination signals
- Tracks episode state transitions and step-by-step action history
- Configures episode settings per task from task.episode_config
- Supports max_steps termination and custom termination conditions
- Session-scoped episode tracking with cleanup on session termination
- Multi-episode support: sessions can have multiple active episodes
- Episode dependency tracking: depends_on_task_id, attached_to_episode_id
- Dependency resolution with retry logic for race conditions
- Validates episode configuration and provides default fallbacks
- Server no longer enforces step limits (client responsibility)
end note

note top of ExecutionManager
**Episode-Based Docker Compose Execution Manager**
Now manages both ephemeral and permanent container environments:
- Episode-scoped execution tracking (not session-scoped)
- SandboxEnvironmentManager: Handles episode-scoped, ephemeral containers
- PermanentEnvironmentManager: Handles server-scoped, persistent containers
- configure_for_task() uses episode_id for proper sandbox isolation
- Automatic network bridging between ephemeral and permanent environments
- Static compose file resolution from environments/sandbox directory
- Enhanced security validation and multi-network executor management
- Permanent services start with server boot and persist across all episodes
- Episode-aware executor factory with episode-specific configurations
- Concurrent execution limits per episode (max_concurrent_per_episode = 3)
- Debug mode support via SABER_DEBUG_MODE environment variable
See command_execution_architecture.puml for complete detailed design.
end note

note bottom of EvaluationManager
**Client-Side Evaluation Storage**
- Server is now dumb storage only - evaluation happens client-side
- Task-based configuration with fail-fast validation
- Evaluation storage via EvaluationStore abstraction
- SessionEvaluationService provides retrieval operations
- Strategy support: static (flag-based), llm_judge (LLM-as-judge)
- Evaluation criteria retrieval for client-side rendering
- No server-side evaluation execution - client performs all scoring
- Logging of session/episode lifecycle events
- No backwards compatibility - fail fast on missing config
end note

